 4. 🖖🏻 1 for the road: Still boldly going 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 The original "Star Trek" cast. Photo: Sunset Boulevard/Corbis via Getty Images Sixty years ago today, "Star Trek" debuted in the U.S., launching a beloved and persistently relevant sci-fi franchise, superfan Alex Fitzpatrick writes. 

 Trek's optimistic view of the future — with co-ed, multiracial, multi- species crews working together to explore strange, new worlds — still resonates today as we grapple with racism, inclusivity, equity and more. 📺 A recent explosion of "New Trek" TV shows brought a fresh generation of fans into the Starfleet fold, despite mixed reviews from some corners.

 Yet the franchise is stuck in unknown space amid owner Paramount's proposed merger with Warner Bros. Discovery. No shows are currently in development or production for the first time in over a decade — though a movie is in the works.

